---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Mythbuster from '../../components/Mythbuster';
---

<Layout title="Cyber Mythbuster: Can I get hacked if...?" description="Interactive flashcards separating cybersecurity fact from Hollywood fiction.">
  <div class="bg-indigo-50 py-12 border-b border-indigo-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-indigo-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
        Cyber Mythbuster
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-indigo-800">
        Hollywood movies make hacking look like magic. Let's separate the facts from the fiction so you know what actually puts you at risk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <Mythbuster client:load />
    
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-12 bg-white border border-slate-200 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm text-center">
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 text-lg">
        The most common way people get "hacked" isn't through complex code or super-viruses. It is through <strong>Social Engineering</strong>—simply tricking you into handing over your password. 
      </p>
      <a href="/tools/scam-decision-tree" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-600 font-bold hover:text-indigo-800 transition-colors text-lg border-b-2 border-indigo-200 hover:border-indigo-600 pb-1">
        Try the "Is It a Scam?" Decision Tree 
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3"></path></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
